    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offensive engine today centers on high-efficiency output from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.85) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs approaching the 5.00 mark. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains our anchor against Quantrill, bolstered by a strong SP skill differential, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives due to an ideal platoon advantage and a premium #2 spot in the order. We are also tracking **Nasim Nunez** (71.50) closely; despite his #8 batting position, his combination of park factors and the exploitable xERA of Young makes him a high-upside play for stolen bases, a category where our aggressiveness remains a key differentiator.\n\nWe faced a tight squeeze at the UTIL/OF slots, ultimately resulting in **Sam Antonacci** (61.12) and **Kyle Tucker** (60.95) securing starts over **Nolan Schanuel** (51.72). **Nolan Schanuel** was the primary consideration for the bench, but his lower raw efficiency against Perkins left him on the outside looking in compared to the dynamic platoon and superior order placement offered by **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the lineup. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** (59.96) remains in the lineup despite a difficult matchup against Griffin; while the platoon disadvantage lowered his base projection, his high-tier plate discipline and spot in the batting order maintain his value above our replacement threshold. \n\nRisk management for this slate focuses on the bottom of our outfield depth, specifically **Jackson Merrill** (53.44) and **Josh Lowe** (52.25). Both face elite arms in Yamamoto and Perkins, respectively, and are subject to lower efficiency caps due to their position in the lineup. While these scores are safer than the <40 \"below floor\" threshold, owners should monitor the wind and in-game adjustments for **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 49.63 is buoyed by favorable weather, but dampened by a challenging encounter with Webb. We will continue to preserve game caps for bench assets like **Josh Jung** and **Dominic Smith** unless late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot.",
